---
/* SUBMIT YOUR TRACK, reescrita 2026-08-16 (pase 12).

   Antes esta pagina vendia los 5 EUR como el lanzamiento a curadores externos,
   que es el servicio GRANDE: eso es playlist pitching y cuesta desde 100 EUR.
   Los 5 EUR son otra cosa, el envio a NUESTRAS listas. Dejarla como estaba
   dejaba dos paginas del mismo sitio prometiendo cosas distintas por el mismo
   dinero.

   NOTA PARA LAS GUARDAS DE LOS .BAT: no escribir aqui, ni en ningun comentario,
   la cadena literal que un .bat vaya a buscar con nocontains. Ya paso el 16/08
   y la comprobacion fallo contra mi propio comentario.

   EL PASO QUE FALLA, Y POR QUE ESTA EN NEGRITA. El cobro va por Ko-fi, y Ko-fi
   no tiene un campo obligatorio para el enlace: el artista lo pega en el mensaje
   del pago o no lo pega. Si no lo pega, hay 5 EUR y no hay cancion. Ese paso es
   el unico modo de fallo real del producto, asi que va numerado, en negrita y
   antes del boton, no en la letra pequena. */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { KOFI, PLAYLISTS_URL, url } from '../../lib/site';
---
<Base
  title="Submit your track"
  description="One Spotify link, 5 EUR, considered for the playlists 109MUSIC runs. Placement is not guaranteed and the playlists are public."
  activeSection="submit">
  <div class="slab">
   <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="kicker mono rise">109MUSIC · Playlists</p>
      <h1 class="display face rise">Submit your<br /><span class="lav">track</span></h1>
      <p class="statement rise">
        One Spotify link, <b>5 EUR</b>, considered for the playlists we run ourselves.
        Placement is not guaranteed, and the playlists are public, so you can check
        whether you fit before you pay.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-cta rise">
        <a class="btn" href={KOFI} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <span>Submit on Ko-fi · 5 EUR</span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href={PLAYLISTS_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <span>Hear the playlists first</span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
   </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section>
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="display">How it works</h2></div>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Pay the 5 EUR on Ko-fi, where we take submissions.</li>
        <li>
          <b>Paste the Spotify link to your track in the message box before you pay.</b>{' '}
          This is the one step that goes wrong. Without the link there is nothing for
          us to listen to, and we have no way of knowing who sent it.
        </li>
        <li>We listen. If it belongs on one of the lists, it goes on.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="keyfact">
        <span class="mono">The five euros buy a listen</span>
        <p>
          They do not buy a placement, and nobody who is honest will sell you one for
          five euros. What they buy is that a person hears the whole track and makes a
          real decision about it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="display">The playlists</h2></div>
      <p class="sec-intro">
        Five lists, around 35,000 likes between them. They are public and they have
        been running for a while, so you can judge them yourself rather than take our
        word for it.
      </p>
      <ul class="aroundlist">
        <li>
          <span class="around-name">Urban Essentials</span>
          <span class="around-line">The main list. Urban, in English and beyond.</span>
          <span class="around-price mono">Public</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="around-name">Urban Spanish Essentials</span>
          <span class="around-line">The same thing in Spanish, and the one most of our own artists live on.</span>
          <span class="around-price mono">Public</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="around-name">Bedroom &amp; chill</span>
          <span class="around-line">Quieter, slower, late. Room for a demo that is not finished-sounding.</span>
          <span class="around-price mono">Public</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="around-name">Zyzz Hardstyle</span>
          <span class="around-line">Gym and workout. Hard, fast, and a completely different audience to the rest.</span>
          <span class="around-price mono">Public</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="around-name">Prod. La Hater</span>
          <span class="around-line">The producer list.</span>
          <span class="around-price mono">Public</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="sec-intro">
        If your record is nowhere near any of those, keep your five euros. We would
        rather tell you here than take it and send you a no.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="sec-head"><h2 class="display">What you do not get</h2></div>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>A guaranteed placement. Anyone promising one is buying it.</li>
        <li>Bot streams, or playlists whose listeners are not real.</li>
        <li>
          Pitching to outside curators. That is the bigger service and it is priced
          differently: <a href={url('/services/#playlist-pitching')}>playlist pitching</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
